{#- BGP_SENTINELS routing policy, as zebra-rs `set` statements.
    Port of dockers/docker-fpm-frr/frr/bgpd/templates/sentinels/policies.conf.j2.

    FRR:

      bgp community-list standard sentinel_community permit <C> no-export
      route-map FROM_BGP_SENTINEL permit 100
       match community sentinel_community
      route-map FROM_BGP_SENTINEL deny 200
      route-map TO_BGP_SENTINEL permit 100

    The community-list line is the part that does not translate word for
    word. One FRR standard community-list entry naming two communities
    matches a route that carries BOTH. A zebra-rs community-set matches a
    route that carries ANY of its members (CommunitySet::matches), so a
    two-member set would accept a route tagged `no-export` alone — which is
    every route a neighbour chose not to export, not just the sentinel's.

    So the conjunction is spelled out: entry 100 matches the sentinel
    community and `call`s a policy that permits only a route carrying
    `no-export`. A callee that denies makes the caller deny, so a route has
    to pass both.

    ASSUMED, NOT MEASURED: that a called policy with no matching entry
    denies, as a route-map does. If it permitted instead, the `no-export`
    half of the test would silently stop applying. Entry 20 states the deny
    explicitly so the result does not rest on that default. -#}
{% if constants.bgp.sentinel_community is defined %}
set community-set sentinel_community members {{ constants.bgp.sentinel_community }}
set community-set sentinel_no_export members no-export
set policy SENTINEL_REQUIRE_NO_EXPORT entry 10 match community sentinel_no_export
set policy SENTINEL_REQUIRE_NO_EXPORT entry 10 action permit
set policy SENTINEL_REQUIRE_NO_EXPORT entry 20 action deny
set policy FROM_BGP_SENTINEL entry 100 match community sentinel_community
set policy FROM_BGP_SENTINEL entry 100 call SENTINEL_REQUIRE_NO_EXPORT
set policy FROM_BGP_SENTINEL entry 100 action permit
{% endif %}
set policy FROM_BGP_SENTINEL entry 200 action deny
set policy TO_BGP_SENTINEL entry 100 action permit
